WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.450
Got indigestion?

2
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.270
Chew an antacid tablet, and it
can help settle your stomach.

3
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:09.850
It reacts with the hydrochloric acid in
your stomach, neutralizing some of it.

4
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.370
And a few minutes later, you
may find yourself burping.

5
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.230
Why can an antacid tablet make you burp?

6
00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:20.590
In this mission, you'll write equations
for acids reacting with oxides,

7
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.550
hydroxides, carbonates and ammonia.

8
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.210
You'll name the parent
acid and base of a salt,

9
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:31.110
and follow the pH as a strong acid
is titrated with a strong base.

10
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.320
Your mission: explain why an
antacid tablet can make you burp.
